      "reference_conclusion": "The stable isotope biplot shows the bulk of the groundwater samples clustering together, but reveals two prominent outliers. One outlier is highly depleted (lowest d18O of -18.21 at a deep well), and the other is notably enriched (highest d18O around -15.54 from a well completed in sediments), indicating divergent recharge or evaporation histories compared to the regional basalt aquifer baseline.",
      "requires_visual_evaluation": true,
      "expected_visual_filename": "isotope_biplot.png",
      "visual_description": "A scatter plot with relative oxygen isotope ratio (d18O) on the x-axis (ranging from approximately -18.5 to -15.0) and hydrogen isotope ratio (d2H) on the y-axis (ranging from roughly -142 to -120). Most points should cluster centrally, with one distinct point isolated in the bottom left corner (most negative values) and one distinct point in the top right corner (least negative values).",
